# 必考词 Unit17
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit17核心词汇

{{narrate}}{{/ˈnæreɪt}}{{v. 叙述；讲述；解说}}{{She narrated the story of her travels in Africa.}}
{{navigate}}{{/ˈnævɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 导航；航行；驾驶}}{{It is difficult to navigate through the dense forest.}}
{{negate}}{{/nɪˈɡeɪt}}{{v. 否定；取消；使无效}}{{His actions negated all the progress we had made.}}
{{neglect}}{{/nɪˈɡlekt}}{{v./n. 忽视；疏忽； neglect}}{{The garden fell into neglect after they moved away.}}
{{negotiate}}{{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt}}{{v. 谈判；协商； negotiate}}{{The two countries are negotiating a peace treaty.}}
{{neutral}}{{/ˈnjuːtrəl}}{{adj. 中立的；中性的}}{{Switzerland remained neutral during the war.}}
{{nevertheless}}{{/ˌnevəðəˈles}}{{adv. 然而；不过； nevertheless}}{{The task was difficult; nevertheless, he completed it on time.}}
{{nominal}}{{/ˈnɒmɪnl}}{{adj. 名义上的；微不足道的； nominal}}{{He holds a nominal position in the company.}}
{{nominate}}{{/ˈnɒmɪneɪt}}{{v. 提名；任命； nominate}}{{She was nominated for the best actress award.}}
{{norm}}{{/nɔːm}}{{n. 标准；规范；常态； norm}}{{Working from home has become the norm.}}
{{notable}}{{/ˈnəʊtəbl}}{{adj. 值得注意的；显著的； notable}}{{The town is notable for its beautiful architecture.}}
{{notion}}{{/ˈnəʊʃn}}{{n. 概念；想法； notion}}{{The notion that the earth is flat has been disproven.}}
{{notwithstanding}}{{/ˌnɒtwɪθˈstændɪŋ}}{{prep./adv. 尽管； notwithstanding}}{{Notwithstanding the rain, the event went ahead as planned.}}
{{nourish}}{{/ˈnʌrɪʃ}}{{v. 养育； nourish；滋养}}{{Good food nourishes the body and mind.}}
{{novel}}{{/ˈnɒvl}}{{adj./n. 新奇的；小说； novel}}{{She came up with a novel approach to the problem.}}
{{nuclear}}{{/ˈnjuːkliər}}{{adj. 核的；原子能的； nuclear}}{{Nuclear energy is a controversial topic.}}
{{numerous}}{{/ˈnjuːmərəs}}{{adj. 众多的； numerous}}{{Numerous studies have shown the benefits of exercise.}}
{{nurture}}{{/ˈnɜːtʃər}}{{v./n. 养育；培养； nurture}}{{Parents should nurture their children's creativity.}}
{{nutrition}}{{/njuˈtrɪʃn}}{{n. 营养；营养学； nutrition}}{{Proper nutrition is essential for good health.}}
{{obey}}{{/əˈbeɪ}}{{v. 服从；遵守； obey}}{{Citizens should obey the law.}}
{{object}}{{/əbˈdʒekt}}{{v. 反对； object}}{{Many residents objected to the new construction plan.}}
{{objective}}{{/əbˈdʒektɪv}}{{n./adj. 目标；客观的； objective}}{{The main objective of the project is to reduce pollution.}}
{{obligate}}{{/ˈɒblɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 使有义务； obligate}}{{The contract obligates both parties to fulfill their duties.}}
{{obligation}}{{/ˌɒblɪˈɡeɪʃn}}{{n. 义务；责任； obligation}}{{You are under no obligation to accept the offer.}}
{{oblige}}{{/əˈblaɪdʒ}}{{v. 迫使；感激； oblige}}{{I would be obliged if you could help me with this.}}
{{obscure}}{{/əbˈskjʊər}}{{adj./v. 模糊的； obscure；使模糊}}{{The meaning of the poem is obscure to most readers.}}
{{observe}}{{/əbˈzɜːv}}{{v. 观察；遵守； observe}}{{Scientists observe the behavior of animals in the wild.}}
{{obsolete}}{{/ˈɒbsəliːt}}{{adj. 过时的； obsolete}}{{The old technology has become obsolete.}}
{{obstacle}}{{/ˈɒbstəkl}}{{n. 障碍； obstacle}}{{Lack of funding is a major obstacle to the project.}}
{{obtain}}{{/əbˈteɪn}}{{v. 获得； obtain}}{{She obtained a degree in computer science.}}
{{obvious}}{{/ˈɒbviəs}}{{adj. 明显的； obvious}}{{The answer was obvious to everyone.}}
{{occasion}}{{/əˈkeɪʒn}}{{n. 场合； occasion}}{{This is a special occasion for the whole family.}}
{{occupy}}{{/ˈɒkjupaɪ}}{{v. 占据； occupy；使忙碌}}{{The meeting occupied the entire morning.}}
{{occur}}{{/əˈkɜːr}}{{v. 发生； occur；出现}}{{The accident occurred at the intersection.}}
{{offend}}{{/əˈfend}}{{v. 冒犯； offend；违反}}{{I'm sorry if my words offended you.}}
{{offset}}{{/ˈɒfset}}{{v./n. 抵消； offset；补偿}}{{The gains offset the losses from the previous quarter.}}
{{offspring}}{{/ˈɒfsprɪŋ}}{{n. 后代； offspring}}{{The lion protects its offspring from danger.}}
{{ongoing}}{{/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ}}{{adj. 进行中的； ongoing}}{{The project is still ongoing.}}
{{operate}}{{/ˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 操作； operate；运转}}{{The machine is easy to operate.}}
{{opponent}}{{/əˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 对手； opponent}}{{She defeated her opponent in the final match.}}
{{opportunity}}{{/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti}}{{n. 机会； opportunity}}{{This is a great opportunity for career development.}}
{{oppose}}{{/əˈpəʊz}}{{v. 反对； oppose}}{{Many citizens opposed the new tax policy.}}
{{opt}}{{/ɒpt}}{{v. 选择； opt}}{{She opted for the cheaper option.}}
{{optimistic}}{{/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk}}{{adj. 乐观的； optimistic}}{{He is optimistic about the future of the economy.}}
{{option}}{{/ˈɒpʃn}}{{n. 选项； option；选择权}}{{We have several options to choose from.}}
{{orient}}{{/ˈɔːrient}}{{v. 使适应； orient；朝向}}{{The program helps new students orient themselves to campus life.}}
{{origin}}{{/ˈɒrɪdʒɪn}}{{n. 起源； origin；出身}}{{The origin of the tradition dates back centuries.}}
{{original}}{{/əˈrɪdʒənl}}{{adj./n. 原始的； original；原件}}{{The original painting is kept in the museum.}}
{{outcome}}{{/ˈaʊtkʌm}}{{n. 结果； outcome}}{{The outcome of the election surprised everyone.}}
{{outlook}}{{/ˈaʊtlʊk}}{{n. 展望； outlook；观点}}{{The economic outlook for next year is positive.}}
{{output}}{{/ˈaʊtpʊt}}{{n. 产量； output；输出}}{{The factory's output has doubled this year.}}
{{outrage}}{{/ˈaʊtreɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 愤怒； outrage；暴行}}{{The decision sparked public outrage.}}
{{overall}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈɔːl}}{{adj./adv. 总体的； overall；总的来说}}{{The overall quality of the product is excellent.}}
{{overcome}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈkʌm}}{{v. 克服； overcome}}{{She overcame many challenges to reach her goal.}}
{{overlook}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈlʊk}}{{v. 忽视； overlook；俯瞰}}{{Don't overlook the small details.}}
{{overseas}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈsiːz}}{{adj./adv. 海外的； overseas}}{{Many students study overseas.}}
{{overt}}{{/əʊˈvɜːt}}{{adj. 公开的； overt}}{{There was no overt sign of hostility.}}
{{overturn}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈtɜːn}}{{v. 推翻； overturn；翻倒}}{{The court overturned the previous ruling.}}
{{overwhelm}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈwelm}}{{v. 压倒； overwhelm；使不知所措}}{{She was overwhelmed by the support from her friends.}}
{{owing}}{{/ˈəʊɪŋ}}{{adj. 欠的； owing to；由于}}{{The match was cancelled owing to bad weather.}}
{{pace}}{{/peɪs}}{{n. 步伐； pace；速度}}{{The pace of change in technology is accelerating.}}
{{panel}}{{/ˈpænl}}{{n. 面板； panel；专家组}}{{A panel of experts reviewed the proposal.}}
{{paradox}}{{/ˈpærədɒks}}{{n. 矛盾； paradox；悖论}}{{It is a paradox that the richest country has the poorest people.}}
{{parallel}}{{/ˈpærəlel}}{{adj./n. 平行的； parallel；类似}}{{The two roads run parallel to each other.}}
{{paralyze}}{{/ˈpærəlaɪz}}{{v. 使瘫痪； paralyze；使麻痹}}{{The accident left him paralyzed from the waist down.}}
{{participate}}{{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 参与； participate}}{{All students are encouraged to participate in the discussion.}}
{{particular}}{{/pəˈtɪkjələr}}{{adj. 特定的； particular；挑剔的}}{{Is there a particular reason you're asking?}}
{{patent}}{{/ˈpætnt}}{{n./adj. 专利； patent；明显的}}{{The company holds several patents for its inventions.}}
{{pattern}}{{/ˈpætn}}{{n. 模式； pattern；图案}}{{Scientists have identified a pattern in the data.}}
{{peculiar}}{{/pɪˈkjuːliər}}{{adj. 独特的； peculiar；奇怪的}}{{There was something peculiar about his behavior.}}
{{perceive}}{{/pəˈsiːv}}{{v. 感知； perceive；认为}}{{The situation is perceived as a crisis by many people.}}
{{percentage}}{{/pəˈsentɪdʒ}}{{n. 百分比； percentage}}{{A large percentage of the population lives in cities.}}
{{period}}{{/ˈpɪəriəd}}{{n. 时期； period；句号}}{{The school period lasts for 45 minutes.}}
{{permanent}}{{/ˈpɜːmənənt}}{{adj. 永久的； permanent}}{{She found a permanent position at the university.}}
{{permit}}{{/pəˈmɪt}}{{v./n. 允许； permit；许可证}}{{Smoking is not permitted inside the building.}}
{{persist}}{{/pəˈsɪst}}{{v. 坚持； persist；持续}}{{He persisted in his efforts despite the difficulties.}}
{{perspective}}{{/pəˈspektɪv}}{{n. 观点； perspective；视角}}{{Try to see the problem from a different perspective.}}
{{pervasive}}{{/pəˈveɪsɪv}}{{adj. 普遍的； pervasive；弥漫的}}{{The influence of social media is pervasive in modern society.}}
{{petition}}{{/pəˈtɪʃn}}{{n./v. 请愿； petition；申请}}{{They signed a petition to save the old building.}}
{{phenomenon}}{{/fəˈnɒmɪnən}}{{n. 现象； phenomenon}}{{Global warming is a serious phenomenon.}}
{{pioneer}}{{/ˌpaɪəˈnɪər}}{{n./v. 先驱； pioneer；开拓}}{{She was a pioneer in the field of genetic research.}}
{{plea}}{{/pliː}}{{n. 请求； plea；辩解}}{{He made a plea for more time to finish the project.}}
{{plead}}{{/pliːd}}{{v. 恳求； plead；辩护}}{{He pleaded not guilty to the charges.}}
{{pledge}}{{/pledʒ}}{{n./v. 誓言； pledge；保证}}{{The government pledged to reduce carbon emissions.}}
{{plunge}}{{/plʌndʒ}}{{v./n. 跳入； plunge；暴跌}}{{Stock prices plunged after the announcement.}}
{{poise}}{{/pɔɪz}}{{n./v. 沉着； poise；平衡}}{{She handled the interview with great poise.}}
{{polar}}{{/ˈpəʊlər}}{{adj. 极地的； polar；截然相反的}}{{The two groups hold polar opposite views.}}
{{policy}}{{/ˈpɒləsi}}{{n. 政策； policy；方针}}{{The government introduced a new education policy.}}
{{polish}}{{/ˈpɒlɪʃ}}{{v./n. 擦亮； polish；润色}}{{She polished her essay before submitting it.}}
{{poll}}{{/pəʊl}}{{n./v. 民意调查； poll；投票}}{{The latest poll shows the incumbent leading.}}
{{ponder}}{{/ˈpɒndər}}{{v. 沉思； ponder；考虑}}{{He pondered the question for a long time.}}
{{popular}}{{/ˈpɒpjələr}}{{adj. 流行的； popular；受欢迎的}}{{The song became very popular among young people.}}
{{populate}}{{/ˈpɒpjuleɪt}}{{v. 居住于； populate；填充}}{{The island is populated by fewer than a hundred people.}}
{{portion}}{{/ˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 部分； portion；一份}}{{A large portion of the budget goes to education.}}
{{pose}}{{/pəʊz}}{{v./n. 摆姿势； pose；造成}}{{Pollution poses a serious threat to public health.}}
{{postpone}}{{/pəˈspəʊn}}{{v. 推迟； postpone}}{{The meeting has been postponed until next week.}}
{{potential}}{{/pəˈtenʃl}}{{adj./n. 潜在的； potential；潜力}}{{The project has great potential for success.}}
{{precede}}{{/prɪˈsiːd}}{{v. 先于； precede}}{{A brief introduction preceded the main lecture.}}
